---
name: fix
description: "Fix a bug: find the root cause, change as little as possible"
category: Write & fix
params:
  mode:
    type: enum
    description: Execution mode
    default: apply
    choices:
      - { value: read, label: Root cause only }
      - { value: suggest, label: Propose a fix }
      - { value: apply, label: Fix it }
  test:
    type: bool
    short: t
    description: Write a failing test first
---
Fix the problem described below.
{% if extra %}

Problem: {{ extra }}
{% endif %}

Requirements:
1. Find the root cause and explain why it happens; don't just treat the symptom.
{% if test %}
2. Before fixing, write a test that reproduces the problem and confirm it fails; confirm it passes after the fix.
{% else %}
2. After fixing, explain how to verify the problem is gone.
{% endif %}
3. Check whether the same root cause exists elsewhere.

{% include "_mode" %}

---
name: perf
description: Performance optimization
category: Write & fix
params:
  focus:
    type: multi
    positional: true
    description: Resources to focus on
    choices:
      - { value: cpu, label: CPU }
      - { value: memory, label: Memory, aliases: [mem] }
      - { value: io, label: I/O }
      - { value: latency, label: Latency }
      - { value: startup, label: Startup time }
  measure:
    type: bool
    default: true
    description: Measure before optimizing
  mode:
    type: enum
    description: Execution mode
    default: suggest
    choices:
      - { value: read, label: Find bottlenecks only }
      - { value: suggest, label: Propose optimizations }
      - { value: apply, label: Optimize directly }
---
Analyze and improve the performance of {% if extra %}{{ extra }}{% else %}this code{% endif %}{% if focus %}, focusing on {% for f in focus %}{{ {"cpu": "CPU", "memory": "memory", "io": "I/O", "latency": "latency", "startup": "startup time"}[f] }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}.

{% if measure %}
Measure first: give a reproducible benchmark or profiling method, use the data to confirm where the bottleneck is, then decide what to optimize. Compare with the same method afterwards.
{% endif %}
List optimizations by payoff, with the expected gain, cost and risk of each. Don't trade readability for small gains.

{% include "_mode" %}

---
name: review
aliases: [r]
description: Code review
category: Review & test
params:
  focus:
    type: multi
    positional: true
    description: What to focus on (multiple allowed)
    choices:
      - { value: correctness, label: Correctness, aliases: [bug] }
      - { value: security, label: Security, aliases: [sec] }
      - { value: performance, label: Performance, aliases: [perf] }
      - { value: maintainability, label: Maintainability, aliases: [maint] }
      - { value: tests, label: Test coverage }
  scope:
    type: enum
    description: Which changes to review
    default: changes
    choices:
      - { value: changes, label: All uncommitted changes }
      - { value: staged, label: Staged changes }
      - { value: branch, label: Current branch }
      - { value: last, label: Last commit }
  strict:
    type: bool
    short: s
    description: "Strict mode: report every doubt"
---
Review {% include "_scope" %}.

Understand the intent of the change before looking for problems.
{% if focus %}
Focus on: {% for f in focus %}{{ {"correctness": "correctness and edge cases", "security": "security (permissions, input validation, secrets, injection)", "performance": "performance and resource usage", "maintainability": "readability and maintainability", "tests": "whether the tests cover the changed behavior"}[f] }}{% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endfor %}.
{% else %}
Pay attention to correctness, edge cases, security and maintainability.
{% endif %}

Output:
1. List issues by severity, each with file and line, the cause, and a suggested fix.
2. Separate confirmed problems from doubts that need verification.
{% if strict %}
3. Strict mode: include anything uncertain and give a confidence level; don't leave things out for brevity.
{% else %}
3. Report only issues that are genuinely worth changing; skip style preferences.
{% endif %}

Do not modify the code.
{% include "_extra" %}

---
name: security
aliases: [sec]
description: Security review
category: Review & test
params:
  focus:
    type: multi
    positional: true
    description: What to check
    choices:
      - { value: auth, label: Authentication and authorization }
      - { value: input, label: Input validation }
      - { value: injection, label: Injection }
      - { value: secrets, label: Secrets }
      - { value: deps, label: Dependencies }
  scope:
    type: enum
    description: Which changes to review
    default: changes
    choices:
      - { value: changes, label: All uncommitted changes }
      - { value: staged, label: Staged changes }
      - { value: branch, label: Current branch }
      - { value: last, label: Last commit }
---
Do a security review of {% include "_scope" %}{% if focus %}, focusing on {% for f in focus %}{{ {"auth": "authentication and access control", "input": "input validation", "injection": "injection (SQL, command, template, path)", "secrets": "leaked keys and sensitive data", "deps": "known vulnerabilities in dependencies"}[f] }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}.

For each finding:
1. Explain how an attacker would exploit it (preconditions and impact), without giving a ready-to-use payload.
2. Rate severity (high / medium / low) and your confidence.
3. Suggest a fix.

Separate confirmed exploitable issues from ones that need further verification. Do not modify the code.
{% include "_extra" %}

---
name: pr
description: Write a pull request description
category: Ship
params:
  sections:
    type: multi
    description: Sections to include
    default: [summary, changes, testing]
    choices:
      - { value: summary, label: Summary }
      - { value: changes, label: Changes }
      - { value: testing, label: Testing }
      - { value: risks, label: Risks and impact }
      - { value: followup, label: Follow-up work }
  lang:
    type: enum
    description: Language
    default: en
    choices:
      - { value: en, label: English }
      - { value: zh, label: Chinese }
  create:
    type: bool
    description: Create the PR with gh
---
Write a pull request description in {{ "Chinese" if lang == "zh" else "English" }} for all changes on the current branch relative to the main branch, with these sections:
{% for s in sections %}
- {{ {"summary": "Summary: what problem this solves and why it's needed", "changes": "Changes: the main changes, grouped by module", "testing": "Testing: how it was verified and which cases are covered", "risks": "Risks and impact: compatibility, migrations, performance", "followup": "Follow-up: what was deliberately left out of this PR"}[s] }}
{% endfor %}

Only include what can be confirmed from the changes. {% if create %}Create the PR with gh pr create when done.{% else %}Output the description only; don't create the PR.{% endif %}
{% include "_extra" %}

---
name: docs
description: Write documentation
category: Ship
params:
  kind:
    type: enum
    positional: true
    description: Kind of document
    default: usage
    choices:
      - { value: api, label: API reference }
      - { value: readme, label: README }
      - { value: usage, label: Usage guide }
      - { value: comments, label: Code comments }
      - { value: changelog, label: Changelog }
  audience:
    type: enum
    description: Audience
    default: developer
    choices:
      - { value: user, label: End users }
      - { value: developer, label: Developers }
---
Write {{ {"api": "an API reference", "readme": "a README", "usage": "a usage guide", "comments": "code comments", "changelog": "a changelog"}[kind] }} for {% if extra %}{{ extra }}{% else %}this code{% endif %}, aimed at {{ "end users" if audience == "user" else "developers" }}.

Requirements:
1. Only write what can be confirmed from the code; flag anything uncertain and ask me.
2. Start with the most common usage example, then the details.
{% if kind == "comments" %}
3. Comments should explain why, not restate what the code does; match the project's existing comment style and density.
{% else %}
3. Follow the format and terminology of the project's existing docs.
{% endif %}
